# APML v2.0.0 - Audio Caching Architecture
# SSI Learning App
# Last Updated: 2026-08-11 (SECURITY INPUT-01: POST /api/audio/batch-urls no longer serves premium past-preview ids to unidentified callers. The gate is unconditional — NOT behind ENTITLEMENT_ENFORCE, which is absent in Vercel production and defaults fail-open — so the bulk shape (500 direct-to-S3 presigned URLs per anonymous request) is closed. bulkAudioDownload now sends a Supabase session or try-link bearer. See offline_download.bulk_download_transport.auth)
# Prev: 2026-08-09 (SCRIPT_VERSION v11 — the walk is MODE-NEUTRAL. Every v10 entry was walked with a mode's caps applied and is a thinned subset in the wrong shape; from v11 one cached script serves Easy and Fast, and a mode toggle never touches any cache. See script_cache)
# Prev: 2026-08-07 (A-86: EVERY client-side walk of an audio-id column now stamps the versioned ref — see versioned_audio_refs.all_client_lanes_stamped)
# Prev: 2026-08-07 (PWA UPDATE never activates a worker under a live page — activation deletes every changed chunk from the precache and kills the running document; skipWaiting/clientsClaim now false in every environment, and directoryIndex:null stops the precache route shadowing navigations. See service_worker + docs/pwa-lifecycle-design.md §2.1a)
# Prev: 2026-08-06 (learning-mode wording: Turbo retired, Easy/Fast are the two modes. PER-CLIP VERSIONED AUDIO REFS documented — the `<uuid>.v<N>` scheme, the server lane (api/_utils/audioAccess.ts → cycles/infplay-cycles) and the client lane (providers/revisedAudioRefs.ts → generateLearningScript), plus why the script-cache drop lane alone could not heal a stale clip. See versioned_audio_refs)
# Prev: 2026-08-04 (intro_audio_missing telemetry — the silence-class that emitted nothing now reports at the fallback point. Earlier: tail-pacing: straggler rounds announce themselves via offlineDlStragglers; stall-proofing: hard per-fetch timeouts + UI liveness rule; readiness THRESHOLD + straggler retry rounds)
# Prev: 2026-07-29 (offline-lease subscription read is FAMILY-AWARE: resolveEffectiveSubscription — a live family member renews on the owner's 'SSi Family' row; see offline_lease.files)
# Prev: 2026-07-27 (content_stamp lane is now STALE-WHILE-REVALIDATE: play the cached script immediately, regenerate in background, fresh applies next session — see content_freshness_stamp)
# Prev: 2026-07-09 (bulk download: presigned URLs resolved JUST-IN-TIME per chunk + TTL-aware expiry recovery — see offline_download.bulk_download_transport. Same day, earlier: offline round 3: behind-position bundle unconditional; listening METADATA cached offline via listeningMetaCache.ts — see offline_download.behind_position / listening_metadata_offline / belt_pill_offline_clarity)
# Prev: 2026-06-16 (offline download now OPEN TO ALL with a free 30-day TASTE for non-payers — "pay for convenience, not content"; reverses the earlier premium hard-gate, the 30-day LEASE plugs the leak by expiry. PLUS the lease is now STATEFUL: offline_leases table = server authority → revocation kill-switch + trial-used memory; renewal is LAZY + weak-signal-safe (timeout/fail-open, never on first load). See premium_gate + offline_lease sections; useEntitlement.offlineRenews, LearningPlayer.canStartOfflineDownload, config/offlineLease.ts, composables/useOfflineLease.ts, api/entitlement/offline-lease.ts, supabase/migrations/20260616_offline_leases.sql)
# Prev: 2026-06-08 (ONE cache-first player; online=offline via cachePlayOnline; rolling filler + AudioCache; AudioPrefetcher/BundleDownloader/usePrefetchManager/OfflineCache/AudioSource all DELETED)

spec audio_caching_architecture:
  version: "3.0.0"
  status: "implemented"
  date: "2026-06-08"

  description: |
    ONE cache-first player. Online == offline: the player only ever reads from the
    cache, and the network's only job is to fill the cache ahead of the playhead.
    cachePlayOnline is default-ON, so an online learner plays cached WAV blobs
    (decoded from cached MP3) exactly like an offline one — the network is only the
    miss fallback for the very first/uncached clip. Audio and text stay atomically
    bound — a Cycle is complete (3 valid audio ids) or it doesn't play.

    Never show connection errors - always keep playing.

    See docs/cold-start-and-playback.md (the live trace) and docs/buffer-model.md
    (SUPERSEDED design intent) for the prose version of this model.

    SUPERSEDED MODULES (deleted — do NOT reference): @ssi/core OfflineCache,
    AudioSource, DownloadManager; cache/AudioPrefetcher; cache/BundleDownloader;
    composables/usePrefetchManager. Their roles are now covered by AudioCache +
    the rolling filler + createAudioCacheSource (below).

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## BACKEND PROXY
  ## ==========================================================================

  backend_proxy:
    endpoint: "/api/audio/:audioId"
    file: "api/audio/[audioId].ts"

    purpose:
      - "Entitlement verification (paid vs free)"
      - "Future CDN flexibility (swap S3 without app update)"
      - "CORS bypass (proper headers from our domain)"
      - "Returns correct 206 ranges for the <audio> element (the SW deliberately stays OUT of the audio path)"

    request_flow:
      1: "Receive audioId (UUID)"
      2: "Query Supabase for S3 key"
      3: "Proxy audio from S3 with caching headers (206 on Range)"
      4: "Return audio stream"

    response_headers:
      Content-Type: "audio/mpeg"
      Cache-Control: "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
      Access-Control-Allow-Origin: "*"

    analytics:
      note: >
        The proxy is NO LONGER a play log. The old audio_plays table was dropped
        2026-05-19 — once playback is cache-first the proxy only ever sees the rare
        cache MISS, so it can't count real plays. Source of truth for "what played"
        is now player_events.audio_play (client-side: user_id, course_code,
        session_id + payload {url, role, legoId, cycleId, cycleType, playbackSpeed}).

    intro_audio_missing:
      file: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/introAudioTelemetry.ts"
      event: "player_events.intro_audio_missing"
      payload: "{legoId, cycleId, cycleType, tier, source}"
      added: "2026-08-04"
      why: >
        A missing presentation clip is not an ERROR anywhere in this system.
        The round-building adapters resolve a prompt URL, get an empty string,
        and SimplePlayer skips a phase with no audio — by design, silently.
        SimplePlayer is also the only emitter of audio_failed. So an
        estate-wide intro-audio gap emitted nothing, anywhere, and surfaced
        months later as a single learner's bug report rather than on the
        health board.
      tiers: >
        known_fallback = no narration, the known clip took the prompt slot
        (degraded but audible). silent = no prompt audio at all — the case
        that reads to a learner as "the intro never played".
      source: "backend (instant-playback cycles endpoint) | script (legacy generateLearningScript)"
      shape: >
        Emitted from the pure adapters (toSimpleRounds, backendCyclesToRounds)
        via a module-level sink LearningPlayer wires to playerLog.event on
        mount and clears on unmount. course_code / session_id / user
        attribution come from the event ROW via usePlayerLog, exactly as
        audio_play does — not duplicated into the payload. Deduped per cycle
        id per session (a round is rebuilt several times per session; the gap
        is a property of the CONTENT). A throwing sink is swallowed —
        telemetry never interferes with playback.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## PER-CLIP VERSIONED AUDIO REFS — how a repaired clip busts every cache
  ## ==========================================================================

  versioned_audio_refs:
    rule: |
      An audio ref is either a bare uuid — "whatever revision is current" — or
      `<uuid>.v<N>`, naming one exact revision. Only clips that have actually
      been revised ever grow a suffix, so unrevised audio keeps its URL and its
      cached bytes and nobody re-downloads a course.

    why_the_revision_rides_in_the_id: |
      There are TWO caches downstream and they key differently. The browser HTTP
      cache keys by URL (a `?v=` query string would bust it). AudioCache keys by
      audio ID and never looks at the URL at all, so a query string would leave
      every learner on stale bytes for good. Versioning the ID moves both,
      because the id IS the cache key AND the thing every `/api/audio/${id}`
      call site interpolates. That is why no player code changed for this: the
      ref is an opaque string that rides through the builders untouched.

    server_lane:
      file: "api/_utils/audioAccess.ts"
      helpers: "parseAudioRef / buildAudioRef / fetchRevisedAudioRefs / stampRowAudioRefs / AUDIO_ID_COLUMNS"
      wired_into:
        - "api/courses/[code]/cycles.ts — the instant-playback bootstrap + tier-3 near-edge rounds"
        - "api/courses/[code]/infplay-cycles.ts"
        - "api/courses/[code]/bundle.ts (no player caller today — tested, not consumed)"
      resolution: "api/audio/[audioId].ts resolves a pinned revision against the course_audio_revisions ledger; a bare ref serves current. batch-urls accepts refs via isValidAudioId."

    client_lane:
      file: "packages/player-vue/src/providers/revisedAudioRefs.ts"
      why: |
        The player does NOT get all its content from the stamped routes.
        generateLearningScript walks course_legos / course_practice_phrases /
        course_seeds / listening_pod_sentences / course_audio DIRECTLY over
        Supabase, and its output is what the script cache stores. The returning-
        learner CACHE FAST PATH in LearningPlayer hydrates SimplePlayer straight
        from that cache and returns — no bootstrap, no round-map, so the tier-3
        /cycles watcher never fires either. A whole session can therefore run
        without ever touching a stamped route.
      rule: |
        The walk fetches the same revised-ref map (one query, in parallel with
        the content queries) and stamps the rows ONCE, before anything copies an
        id onto a ScriptItem. Any future client-side reader of a *_audio_id
        column must do the same, or it reintroduces the stale-clip bug.
      drop_lane_is_not_enough: |
        Dropping the script cache on an audio_stamp move does NOT heal an
        unstamped walk — the regenerated script is just as stale as the one it
        replaced. This was the live German symptom on 2026-08-06: the repair,
        the stamp and the drop lane all fired correctly and the learner still
        heard pre-repair audio. SCRIPT_VERSION v10 orphans the v9 entries.
      shared_map: |
        getRevisedAudioRefs(supabase, courseCode) — ONE in-flight query per
        course, shared by every lane. An EMPTY result is deliberately not
        memoised: empty means either "no revised clips" or "the lookup failed",
        the two are indistinguishable by design, and caching a failure would
        strand a whole session on bare refs. clearRevisedAudioRefs() drops it.

      array_id_columns: |
        stampRowAudioRefs also walks sentence_audio_ids /
        sentence_known_audio_ids on listening_pod_sentences. Those ids become
        the per-sentence target/known clips after the silence-split flatten, so
        leaving them bare would defeat the stamping of the row they came from.
        bareAudioId(ref) strips `.vN` back for any lookup that must go to the
        DATABASE — course_audio is keyed by the bare uuid.

      all_client_lanes_stamped:
        - "providers/generateLearningScript.ts — the script walk (original consumer)"
        - "composables/usePodLapScheduler.ts — listening_pod_sentences + bookends, stamped after the offline fallback resolves"
        - "composables/useLayer1Scheduler.ts — course_seeds + bookends, same position"
        - "composables/listeningMetaCache.ts — the OFFLINE listening snapshot, and it now refreshes on an AUDIO stamp move as well as a content stamp move (a clip repair moves audio_stamp and not necessarily content_stamp, so the content lane alone would leave a downloaded snapshot on the pre-repair ref forever). Load-bearing: offline the ref lookup cannot run, so the schedulers' own stamping degrades to a no-op; the snapshot must be written stamped while online or an offline learner plays pre-repair audio for its whole life. clipTexts is queried by bare id and keyed by the stamped ref"
        - "components/ListeningOverlay.vue — its four own walks: fine-knowns, USE phrases, seeds, and the offline listening pack's id list"
        - "components/PronunciationOverlay.vue — its course_practice_phrases walk"
        - "providers/CourseDataProvider.ts — every walk, via the private revisedRefs() accessor: session items, welcome, presentation (single + batch), baskets, lego range"
        - "composables/usePodStage0.ts — drives the PodStageAuditioner QA surface; a QA surface that plays the pre-repair clip is a QA surface that lies"

      already_covered_no_change_needed:
        - "composables/useFullCourseScript.ts (CourseExplorer) — builds URLs from generateLearningScript output, which is stamped upstream"

      still_unstamped_by_design:
        - "useScriptCache's direct-to-bucket getAudioUrl fallback — bypasses /api/audio entirely; s3_key is current, so it is fresh-by-accident, not by design"
        - "shared_audio rows (instructions, encouragements) in CourseDataProvider — cross-course template table, outside the per-course course_audio revision ledger"

      stamp_at_the_walk_not_the_url: |
        Standing rule for any future client-side reader of a *_audio_id column:
        stamp where the ROWS are fetched, never at the URL builder. The fetched
        rows are what flows into the script cache, the schedulers and the
        offline snapshot, so a last-moment URL rewrite leaves the bare id sitting
        in cached state upstream — which is the bug, not the symptom.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## THE CACHE — AudioCache (one IndexedDB store, two lifecycles)
  ## ==========================================================================

  audio_cache:
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/AudioCache.ts"
    interface: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/AudioCache.types.ts"
    db: "ssi-audio-cache-v2 (IndexedDB, single 'audio' store keyed by audio id)"
    purpose: "App-controlled, readable cache for both online cache-play and offline play"

    structure: >
      ONE object store, one row per audio id (blob + mimeType + size + lifecycle +
      cachedAt/lastAccessedAt). A `lifecycle` column distinguishes two namespaces;
      in-memory id Sets (persistentIds / ephemeralIds) make has(id) synchronous.
      Self-heals a storeless DB (interrupted upgrade / ?reset) by delete + recreate.

    namespaces:
      persistent:
        purpose: "Course-spanning warm cache — the rolling filler and pods/L1/warmFirstKnownAudio write here"
        api: "ensure(id) | has(id) | getBlobUrl(id) | evictToTarget(targetBytes)"
        eviction: "persistentEvictToTarget — LRU by lastAccessedAt, deletes oldest persistent rows until under the byte cap (this is the offline depth cap / quota self-trim)"
        promotion: "an id already cached as ephemeral is rewritten in place to persistent (no re-fetch)"
      ephemeral:
        purpose: "Per-LEGO build sets (acquireForLego / releaseForLego, abortable)"
        status: >
          VESTIGIAL — kept for now but NO production callers remain (only the test
          suite acquires/releases ephemeral sets). The rolling filler writes
          persistent only. Treat as dead weight pending removal.

    read_paths:
      getBlobUrl: "mp3 blob: URL — re-wraps to carry mimeType so iOS Safari can decode it"
      getWavBlobUrl: >
        Decode the cached mp3 bytes and re-encode to a WAV blob: URL (bytesToWavBlob,
        cache/wav.ts). THIS is the cache-first / offline play read path: WebKit's
        <audio> rejects mp3 blob: URLs ('operation is not supported') but plays WAV.
        Decoded once per id into an in-memory wavUrlCache and reused (spaced rep
        replays the same clips), so we never decode the same audio twice. WAV is NOT
        a persisted tier — it's just-in-time and in-memory.

    quota:
      quotaPressure: "navigator.storage.estimate() usage/quota ratio (0..1) — drives self-trim before the browser errors"
      stats: "per-namespace count+bytes (5s TTL cache) + quota/usage — used by the offline size estimate"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## AUDIO SOURCE ADAPTER — createAudioCacheSource
  ## ==========================================================================

  audio_source:
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/createAudioCacheSource.ts"
    purpose: "Read-path bridge: gives RealAudioController a getAudioUrl(audioRef) over AudioCache"

    wiring: >
      createAudioCacheSource(audioCache, courseCode, () => offlinePlaybackActive() || cachePlayOnline)
      in LearningPlayer.vue. The 3rd arg (shouldServeBlobs) is the cache-first gate.

    resolution:
      when_serving_blobs: "getWavBlobUrl(id) → WAV blob: URL from cache; null on miss → fall through to network URL"
      otherwise: "return audioRef.url unchanged (streaming path; only used with ?stream=1)"
      note: >
        The main 4-phase cycle resolves through resolveAudioUrl / resolveCachedPlaybackUrl
        (cache/resolvePlaybackUrl.ts) — the same id→lock-safe-playable-URL substrate the
        listening overlay plays through. createAudioCacheSource serves AudioController's
        OTHER audio (intro, welcome, commentary, pod laps, dialogues).

  cache_play_online:
    flag: "const cachePlayOnline = !URLSearchParams(location.search).has('stream')  (LearningPlayer.vue)"
    default: "ON — online learners play cached WAV blobs, exactly like offline"
    bypass: "?stream=1 forces the legacy streaming path for comparison"
    why: >
      Keeping the MAIN cycle off the network (cache blob, not a streamed range) is what
      survives iOS lock/background. Streaming put the network back in the play path and
      drained the buffer; cache-play removes that.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## THE ROLLING FILLER — how the cache is kept ahead of the playhead
  ## ==========================================================================

  rolling_filler:
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue"
    purpose: "Network's only job: fill AudioCache.persistent ~20 min ahead of the playhead"

    spans:
      ROLLING_SPAN_MS: "20 * 60 * 1000 — steady deep fill, concurrency 1 (gentle)"
      BURST_SPAN_MS:   "10 * 60 * 1000 — fast head warm, concurrency 3 (cold-start / restart)"

    mechanism:
      expandScript: "grows the loaded script ahead (ensureLiveSpanLoaded) so we warm a DEEP cache, not just the bootstrap window — also extends INF-PLAY / revival tails"
      fillBuffer: >
        Builds ONE ordered missing-list [cycles…, pods…, L1…], dedupes, and a
        missing-only worker drains it front-to-back via audioCache.persistent.ensure(id).
        Structural priority (no rate measurement): every uncached cycle warmed before any
        pod, every pod before any L1 listening clip. Silent on error — the play path
        handles any miss by streaming that one clip.
      triggers:
        - "first rounds load → warmBurst (BURST span, concurrency 3)"
        - "each round advance → fillRollingBuffer (ROLLING span, concurrency 1)"
        - "stop/pause → warmBurst (so a restart is instant)"
      keep_warming_while_locked: >
        fillBuffer KEEPS warming even while hidden/locked (a 63-min locked run streamed
        the whole time and never died — going network-silent on lock just drained the
        buffer and forced streaming anyway). Yields on isOnline false (offline mode owns
        true-offline) and on an active bulk download.

    next_cycle_warm:
      file: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/SimplePlayer.ts"
      method: "prefetchNextCycle() — warms the next cycle's known (priority high) + voice1/voice2 (low) so the head is never a miss"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## SERVICE WORKER — deliberately OUT of the audio path
  ## ==========================================================================

  service_worker:
    file: "packages/player-vue/vite.config.js (VitePWA / Workbox)"
    audio: >
      The SW does NOT cache audio. The old CacheFirst on /api/audio/* was REMOVED
      2026-05-24 — the SW (and Vercel's edge) served cached full-200 bodies in
      response to <audio> Range requests, which iOS Safari can't handle (plays ~0.5s
      then stalls forever), and it flapped working/broken across SW versions. Audio
      now goes straight to the origin proxy (correct 206s). globIgnores excludes
      mp3/wav/ogg/m4a from precache; cleanupOutdatedCaches clears runtime caches on
      activate. AudioCache (IndexedDB) is the app-controlled cache, fully independent
      of the SW.
    what_sw_still_does:
      - "Precache the app shell (js/css/html/svg/woff2)"
      - "NetworkFirst on document navigations (3s timeout → cache) so deploys propagate — real since 2026-08-07: directoryIndex:null stops the precache route shadowing '/' navigations"
      - "CacheFirst on Google Fonts (fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com) only"
      - "skipWaiting/clientsClaim FALSE in EVERY environment (registerType:'prompt'). The app never activates a waiting worker: activation deletes every changed chunk from the precache, so a live page loses its own code and dies at its next lazy import. Taking an update is a plain reload; the worker takes over once no client is open. See docs/pwa-lifecycle-design.md §2.1a"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## OFFLINE DOWNLOAD — DEPTH PICKER
  ## ==========================================================================

  offline_download:
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue"
    purpose: "Deliberate, opt-in download of upcoming course content for offline play"

    depth_unit:
      measure: "% of course content (rounds ahead of the cursor)"
      NOT: "playback time"
      why: >
        Offline never STOPS — when the downloaded content runs out it drops into
        INF PLAY and recycles the cache forever, so 'hours offline' is infinite
        regardless of download size. The knob controls how much NEW course
        material you carry, not how long you can listen.
      behind_position: >
        UNCONDITIONAL (2026-07-09): the bundle ALWAYS includes every main-flow
        round from the COURSE START up to the cursor, on top of the slider's
        ahead-span. A fresh device mid-course (account sync) has none of the
        earlier belts' audio cached, so a cursor-forward-only bundle left them
        dead offline despite "downloaded course" (Tom's airplane-mode test).
        Slider semantics unchanged — it only chooses the NEW learning carried;
        the MB estimate counts behind + ahead, and the picker says "Plus
        everything up to where you are — included automatically".

    flow:
      - "Tapping 'Offline mode' closes the mode tray (handleOffline) and opens the 'Take it offline' picker (showOfflinePicker)"
      - "Picker = a notched SLIDER (how much of what's left to carry) + a live MB readout + a course-depth bar"
      - "Tapping Download → startOfflineDownload() → sets offlineActive, downloads the selected depth"
      - "Turning offline off revokes blob URLs and resets state"

    single_popup_rule:
      requirement: "The input dialog must ALWAYS be accessible — one popup at a time."
      why: >
        The mode tray lives inside the bottom-nav's z-index:3000 stacking context;
        the picker teleports to <body>. Two things keep the dialog reachable:
      how:
        - "ModeTray.handleOffline closes the tray on the offline tap, so the picker is the only popup"
        - "offline-picker-backdrop z-index 3100 — above the nav/belt-skip/paywall layer (3000), below system prompts (PWA update/install)"
        - "Dialog capped at max-height calc(100dvh - 48px): header + note pinned, options scroll → every control reachable on short/landscape screens"
        - "Dismiss via ✕, backdrop tap, or Escape (matches the app's other modals)"

    depth_slider:
      control: "notched <input type=range> (offlineNotchIndex 0..5) + tappable tick labels"
      notches: "[0.02, 0.05, 0.10, 0.25, 0.50, 1]  # OFFLINE_NOTCHES"
      unit: >
        Fraction of the REMAINING course (cursor → tail), NOT of the whole course.
        So the top notch (100%) always means 'the rest of the course' regardless
        of how far through you are, and notches never collapse into each other —
        no per-notch hiding needed. Thumb starts at the smallest (2%) on each open.
      mapping: "offlineSelectedRounds = frac>=1 ? poolRounds : ceil(poolRounds·frac), min 1"
      pool: >
        offlinePoolRounds: mid-course = total − start (new content ahead);
        finished/INF-PLAY (start >= total, cursor at/past the main-loop tail) =
        the whole course (no new content left — download = keep it offline to
        recycle); unknown length = roundsLoadedAhead. NEVER 0 while total>0
        (was the bug: courseTotalRounds is main-loop-only, so a finished learner
        had remaining=0 → every notch collapsed to one round). offlineAtTail flips
        the slider/bar/labels to the 'keep N% of the course offline' framing.
      why_not_time: >
        Time is misleading twice: INF PLAY makes total offline time infinite, and
        the 'new' portion stretches with replay and with the learner's mode
        (Easy doubles the reps). So the readout is MB (real
        cost) + a course-depth bar (the pre-INF-PLAY new learning made visible),
        never a duration.
      course_depth_bar: >
        offlineCourseBar — donePct (start/total, already learned) + newPct
        (selectedRounds/total, the new chunk carried). Untinted remainder = where
        INF PLAY recycling lives. % is of the WHOLE course here (for honest depth).

    size_estimate:
      shown_for_selected_notch: "≈MB, split '≈X MB new + Y MB catch-up' (offlineSelectedEstimate); quick basis on open, truth pass settles it within seconds"
      bytes_per_file: "avg from audioCache.stats() (persistent.bytes / count), fallback ~24KB"
      files_projection: >
        TRUE-manifest enumeration (founder ruling 2026-07-31 — the 2% pick
        showed ≈48 MB while the real download was 9,742 files): a background
        truth pass expands the script (same machinery as the download) and
        counts the aux listening/dialogues bundle's missing files
        (auxMissing). The readout then counts, per notch, exactly the ids the
        download will fetch (collectRoundsAudioIds, deduped) that are NOT
        already cached — split into 'new' (the slider's slice) and 'catch-up'
        (behind-position prefix + aux bundle). Cached-aware by construction:
        a re-download reads 'Already downloaded ✓'. The old avg-files/round ×
        rounds heuristic is gone — it couldn't see cross-round clip reuse and
        omitted the aux bundle entirely.
      device_quota: "navigator.storage.estimate() via audioCache.stats().quotaBytes"
      accuracy: "best-effort, labelled '≈'; numbers may grow for a few seconds while the truth pass expands the script, then hold exact-at-estimate-time"

    key_functions:
      courseTotalRounds: "course length (main-loop), the % denominator"
      roundsForCourseFraction: "fraction → round count ahead, capped at course tail; >=1 → Infinity"
      ensureOfflineRoundsLoaded: "expandScript() until the behind-position prefix (round 1 → cursor) is loaded AND N rounds loaded ahead, or generator dry"
      behindPositionRoundsLoaded: "cachedRounds[0].roundNumber === 1 — round numbers are course-global 1-based on every producer, so this detects a cursor-anchored bootstrap window that still needs the full walk"
      collectRoundsAudioIds: "unique /api/audio ids over [course start … cursor + N rounds ahead] — behind-position always included"
      downloadForOffline: "(roundsAhead) — ensure + collect + fetch missing into IndexedDB"

    bulk_download_transport:
      file: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/bulkAudioDownload.ts"
      purpose: >
        Transport layer for downloadForOffline / INF-PLAY bulk fetches: resolves
        ids to presigned S3 GET URLs in batches (POST /api/audio/batch-urls,
        cap 500 ids, ~5-min TTL) and fetches bytes directly from S3 at high
        concurrency (24 idle / 6 playing), skipping the per-clip serverless
        proxy hop. Proxy path (12 / 4) remains the fallback for endpoint
        failure, denied ids, and clips whose direct fetch fails.
      auth: >
        SECURITY (INPUT-01, 2026-08-11): batch-urls denies premium
        past-preview ids to callers it cannot identify, unconditionally — NOT
        behind ENTITLEMENT_ENFORCE (absent in production, defaults fail-open).
        This module therefore sends an Authorization bearer: the Supabase
        session access_token when signed in, else a live `ssi-try-token`
        entitlement token, else no header. Free/community courses and preview
        seeds (<= Yellow, seed 19) are never gated, so anonymous guests keep
        full bulk download of everything they may have. The per-clip proxy
        keeps its fail-open posture — `<audio src>` cannot send a header.
      jit_url_resolution: >
        Presigned URLs are requested JUST-IN-TIME, one chunk at a time: resolve
        chunk → download chunk to completion → resolve next chunk. Never
        resolve all chunks upfront — the v3 bundle takes longer than the 5-min
        TTL on real connections, so upfront resolution meant every clip after
        the TTL hit an expired URL → S3 403 → 3 wasted retries + backoff on a
        dead URL → slow proxy tail (Tom's on-device stutter, 2026-07-09).
      ttl_handling: >
        The endpoint's ttlSeconds (default 300) is honoured with a 60% safety
        margin. A chunk that outlives the margin mid-download (slow network,
        suspended tab) gets its REMAINING ids batch re-requested before
        dispatch. An individual fetch that fails expired-looking (403 in the
        error, or URL past the margin) is NEVER retried on the same URL:
        exactly one fresh-URL re-request for that id, then proxy fallback.
        withRetry (3 attempts, linear backoff) still covers genuinely
        transient errors on non-expired URLs.
      straggler_rounds: >
        A clip that exhausts its in-pass retries is NOT final: the run ends
        with up to 3 straggler rounds — every still-missing id re-run as a
        fresh pass (new presigned URLs, 2s/8s/20s backoff between rounds)
        before anything is counted failed. bulkDownloadAudio returns
        { completed, failedIds } so the caller can keep retrying the tail in
        the background. Founder repro 2026-07-31: 10 of 9,742 transiently
        failing must never conclude a download. Each straggler round fires
        counters.onStragglerRound(remaining) → offlineDlStragglers, so the
        tray copy flips to "Finishing up — checking the last N clips…"
        instead of sitting on a near-frozen 99% (founder tail-pacing
        report, 2026-07-31); stalled copy still wins if progress truly
        stops for 20s.
      fetch_timeouts: >
        Every network wait in the download path has a hard ceiling — a hung
        fetch (wedged connection) otherwise never settles, freezing the whole
        run at a fixed percentage with no display change (founder stall at
        91%, 2026-07-31). AudioCache.doFetchAndStore aborts any audio fetch
        (headers + body, presigned OR proxy) after fetchTimeoutMs (default
        30s), which also clears the in-flight de-dupe entry so retries fetch
        for real instead of reusing the dead promise; fetchBatchAudioUrls
        aborts the batch-urls POST after 20s and returns null (proxy
        fallback). A timeout is a rejection the existing retry/straggler
        machinery already handles — a stall can cost at most ~30s, never
        forever.
      tested: "bulkAudioDownload.test.ts — incl. JIT interleaving (no upfront resolution), 403→fresh-URL recovery without proxy fallback, mid-chunk TTL-margin batch refresh via an injected clock, straggler rounds healing a transient tail, the N-10-of-N permanently-dead shape completing with exact failedIds, and a hanging batch-urls POST resolving null at the timeout; AudioCache.test.ts covers the hung-fetch timeout + inflight-cleared retry"

    listening_metadata_offline:
      file: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/listeningMetaCache.ts"
      purpose: >
        The Listening overlay (Dialogues/Core), the pod-lap scheduler and the
        L1 scheduler read their STRUCTURE (listening_pod_sentences rows, Core
        seed list, bookends, pod_fine_known map, LEGO catalogue) live from
        Supabase. The download cached the AUDIO but not this metadata — so in
        airplane mode the overlay showed "listening_pod_sentences: TypeError:
        Load failed" and Core spun on a dead fetch (Tom 2026-07-09).
      write: >
        downloadForOffline → collectAuxiliaryAudioIds →
        collectListeningModeAudioIds → fetchAndCacheListeningMeta persists ONE
        all-or-nothing entry per course to IndexedDB (ssi-listening-meta,
        same pattern as the script cache). The listening bundle's audio ids
        (collectListeningMetaAudioIds) are DERIVED from those same rows —
        Core seeds, pod turns, per-sentence split clips, explainers, Take-G
        fusion slices, fine-known glosses, bookends — so metadata and audio
        can never drift apart. (Take-G + fine-known clips joined the bundle
        here: with metadata cached, Drill's fusion rungs are reachable
        offline, so their audio must be too.)
      read: >
        Network-first with cache fallback everywhere; cache-first when
        navigator.onLine === false (no doomed fetch, no error noise).
        Readers: useListeningPods (rows + split-clip texts), ListeningOverlay
        loadSeeds (Core list), usePodLapScheduler.initialize (rows +
        bookends + fine-knowns; Stage-0 clip-map load is now try/caught —
        offline just skips the Stage-0 prepend), useLayer1Scheduler.initialize
        (seeds + catalogue + bookends).
      not_downloaded_state: >
        Offline with NO cached entry → explicit copy ("Dialogues/Core aren't
        downloaded yet — connect once and download for offline…"), never an
        infinite spinner or a raw TypeError. Entry-present always means
        fully-usable (all-or-nothing write). Tested in
        listeningMetaCache.test.ts (fake-indexeddb, incl. the useListeningPods
        offline fallback both ways).

    content_freshness_stamp:
      files: >
        supabase/migrations/20260722_course_content_stamp.sql,
        packages/player-vue/src/composables/useScriptCache.ts
        (checkContentVersion), listeningMetaCache.ts
        (refreshListeningMetaIfStale)
      purpose: >
        Structural self-invalidation for the metadata caches. Content fixed in
        the DB used to be served stale from devices for MONTHS (the ita
        'come'='how' gloss: fixed 2026-03-12, still shown 2026-07-22) because
        invalidation was a hand-bumped version string (META_VERSION /
        SCRIPT_VERSION) nobody remembers to move.
      mechanism: >
        courses.content_stamp (timestamptz) is TRIGGER-maintained — any
        insert/update/delete on course_seeds, course_legos,
        course_practice_phrases, course_audio, listening_pod_sentences or
        lego_introductions moves it (debounced to one bump per transaction;
        exception-safe so stamping can never break a content write).
        checkContentVersion's existing boot query selects it alongside
        content_version (no new request). Each cache entry records the stamp
        it was built from; mismatch while ONLINE → STALE-WHILE-REVALIDATE
        (founder ruling 2026-07-27 — the earlier drop-and-regenerate blocked
        first play behind a full-course walk, 20-24s observed on device):
        the entry is KEPT and marked stale (getScriptStaleness); the session
        plays the cached script immediately; LearningPlayer regenerates on
        idle (runSwrRevalidation) and writes the fresh script + a
        'Your course was updated' notice flag for the NEXT session.
        Corrections land one session later — accepted trade. The offline
        LEASE carries over any rewrite that brings no leases of its own
        (setCachedScript read-before-write — entitlement state, not script
        state). Queue-derived cache writes (offline-download persists) pass
        the in-memory rounds' own vintage stamp so an SWR session never
        mis-stamps old rounds as fresh; the listening bundle still refetches
        in the background. Entries with no stamp (pre-mechanism devices) are
        stale-once — now healed via the same non-blocking SWR path.
        cold_start telemetry carries scriptPath
        (cache|swr|progressive|infplay_cache|full) and script_revalidated
        records each background regeneration.
      offline: >
        No stamp is obtainable offline (the courses query fails) → nothing
        invalidates. A stale cache OFFLINE is correct behaviour; staleness
        only matters once online. META_VERSION/SCRIPT_VERSION remain as the
        schema-SHAPE escape hatch (key format changes), no longer the content
        freshness mechanism. content_version (hand-bumped semver) keeps its
        heavier role: audio regeneration → full clear incl. SW audio cache.
      tested: >
        useScriptCache.contentStamp.test.ts (SWR keep-and-mark-stale,
        revalidation-write clears staleness, vintage-preserving write keeps
        it, lease carry-over) + listeningMetaCache.test.ts, and live e2e
        e2e/repro-stale-cache-refresh.mjs (doctored stale-vintage IndexedDB
        entries structurally refreshed on online boot against the real DB)
        + e2e/swr-course-load-walk.mjs (deployed-build walk: cold boot is
        progressive, doctored-stale reload plays from cache with
        scriptPath='swr' + script_revalidated on the telemetry wire, next
        open shows the course-updated notice — PASS vs the dev alias
        2026-07-27: swr reload 2.9s vs the 20-24s blocking regen it
        replaces; background revalidation 8.5s).

    belt_pill_offline_clarity:
      file: "packages/player-vue/src/components/ProgressModal.vue"
      source_of_truth: >
        offlineUnavailableBeltNames (LearningPlayer) — a belt is available
        offline iff its landing round has ≥1 cycle whose audio is ACTUALLY in
        the persistent cache (unchanged; it was correct, just visually
        ambiguous).
      visual: >
        Unavailable pills: hard dim + greyscaled dot + dashed border + a
        padlock glyph overlay (map-chip-lock). Available pills fully normal.
        0.4 opacity alone read as "murky as hell what was ready to play"
        on-device (Tom 2026-07-09).
      hint: >
        With the behind-position bundle the downloaded ladder is contiguous
        from the start, so the modal hint names the edge exactly:
        "offline — belts up to <X> ready to play; beyond needs a connection"
        (offlineReadyUpToBeltName = last belt before the first unavailable).

    premium_gate:
      requirement: >
        Offline download is OPEN TO EVERYONE on EVERY course (incl. free/community);
        non-payers get a free 30-day TASTE, then pay to keep it. We sell the
        CONVENIENCE of offline, never the content — community courses are free to
        learn forever (online, and the first 30 days offline).
      model: >
        REVERSES the earlier hard-gate (where offline download was premium-only).
        The 30-day lease now closes the "download once, never return" leak BY
        EXPIRY instead of by blocking the download — so the door can open and become
        a taste-then-convert funnel (esp. valuable for the India-first push where
        data is expensive). Decision 2026-06-16, Tom: "community courses are always
        and forever free, but you pay for convenience."
      why: >
        Online play to Yellow stays free (gateSeed). Offline download is free to
        START for all; the lease governs longevity — payers renew, non-payers get a
        single 30-day taste. The leak (free offline forever) is plugged by the lease
        lapsing, not by a download paywall.
      where: >
        useEntitlement.canDownloadOffline(course) now returns true for everyone (the
        door). useEntitlement.offlineRenews(course) = the OLD gate (active sub /
        full|course entitlement / admin-tester-god) — does this user's offline RENEW
        vs being a 30-day taste; drives the trial UI + the re-download paywall.
        LearningPlayer.canStartOfflineDownload() is the trigger gate (toggleOffline
        before the picker, startOfflineDownload, startOfflineDownloadInfPlay): payers
        always pass; a non-payer passes on first download ('none') or mid-trial
        ('valid') but is sent to showPaywall once the taste has LAPSED ('expired' /
        'clock-untrusted') — re-downloading then would silently reset the taste (and
        re-bill egress), so that is the conversion moment.
      ui: >
        ModeTray Offline row: toggle is always live (no premium lock badge — removed);
        offlineTrial (shared ref, = !offlineRenews) nudges "Free offline for 30 days".
        Lock overlay copy branches on offlineTrial: payer = "reconnect to unlock";
        trial = "free offline trial ended — subscribe to keep your downloads".
      caveat: >
        The lease is client-side (IndexedDB), so a determined non-payer can reset the
        taste by clearing storage / re-downloading. Acceptable for v1 (low-value:
        it's free content's offline convenience). The deferred server-side
        offline_leases table (see offline_lease.deferred) is the full fix if abuse
        appears; an egress cap on the free-tier download depth is the other lever.

    offline_lease:
      requirement: "Spotify-style 30-day lease — downloads re-validate online or lock. STATEFUL (v2): the server is the per-course authority."
      files:
        - "config/offlineLease.ts — LEASE_DAYS=30, computeExpiry, isLeaseValid, isClockTrustworthy, leaseStatus (+ 'revoked'), leaseShouldRevalidate, RENEW_AHEAD_MS/STALE_AFTER_MS/MIN_RENEW_INTERVAL_MS/VALIDATE_TIMEOUT_MS (pure, unit-tested in offlineLease.test.ts — 20 tests)"
        - "composables/useOfflineLease.ts — LAZY renew (gated; reconnect/6h-timer/deferred-boot-tick) + lock/unlock; consumes server per-course authority (shared singleton, wired once in App.vue)"
        - "api/entitlement/offline-lease.ts — STATEFUL server authority over the offline_leases table: POST {courses[]} → per-course {leaseExpiresAt, isTrial, revoked, entitlementExpiresAt}; serverNow is the clock anchor; FALLS BACK to the old stateless shape if the table is absent. Subscription read is FAMILY-AWARE (2026-07-29): resolveEffectiveSubscription (api/_utils/familyAccess.ts) — own row first, else a live family member resolves the owner's active 'SSi Family' row, so members' downloads RENEW like payers'"
        - "supabase/migrations/20260616_offline_leases.sql — offline_leases table (learner_id, course_code, expires_at, is_trial, revoked_at, …; unique(learner_id,course_code); RLS own-row select; APPLIED to shared DB)"
        - "useScriptCache.ts — lease stored on CachedScript.offlineLease (no new store); getOfflineLease/setOfflineLease/getAllOfflineLeases patch it in place"
      authority: >
        offline_leases is the server's per-course record. Payer (sub/full|course
        entitlement/admin) → RENEWS (+30d, is_trial=false). Non-payer → a single
        non-renewing 30-day TASTE (is_trial=true); the row persists after it lapses
        so a storage-wipe + re-download is recognised as TRIAL-USED, not a fresh
        taste. revoked_at set (admin: refund/chargeback) → locked regardless.
      grant: "downloadForOffline / startOfflineDownloadInfPlay end → grantLease(course, entitlementExpiryClamp) stamps a local optimistic lease THEN forces a background validate (POST) that creates the server row + returns authoritative expiry"
      renew: >
        LAZY — NOT on first load. maybeRenew() is gated by leaseShouldRevalidate
        (only near expiry / >1d stale) + online + a throttle, so a user with runway
        makes ZERO calls. Each successful validate adopts the server's leaseExpiresAt
        (or, in stateless fallback, slides serverNow+30d locally). Forced only on a
        deliberate reconnect / grant / boot self-heal.
      weak_signal: >
        The Spotify "half-connected gets bent out of shape" fix: every validate has
        a hard VALIDATE_TIMEOUT_MS abort and fails OPEN; the boot/self-heal check is
        NON-BLOCKING (checkOfflineLease reads only local IndexedDB, kicks any renew in
        the background); the throttle stops online/offline flapping from spamming.
        Airplane mode never even tries.
      lock: >
        isCourseLeaseValid(course) gates offlinePlaybackActive(): expired/revoked/
        clock-wound-back → false. Bytes are PRESERVED; a successful renew unlocks.
        Overlay copy branches payer ('reconnect to unlock') vs trial ('subscribe').
      cardinal_sin_guards:
        fail_open: "infra/auth/TIMEOUT failure → keep the existing lease, retry later. Never lock a user who can't be checked."
        graceful_tail: "lapsed sub (not entitled, not revoked) → server doesn't slide; the remaining days run out, no instant cut (§5 default a)."
        clock_tamper: "a device clock wound back before lastValidatedAt → clock-untrusted → locked (server serverNow is the renew anchor)."
        dev_demo_bypass: "ssi-demo-tier / dev paid flags → infinite lease, never locks."
        entitlement_clamp: "lease can't outlive a time-boxed entitlement code (server clamps expires_at = min(now+30d, code expiry))."
      revocation: "admin SQL: update offline_leases set revoked_at = now() where learner_id = '<uuid>' [and course_code='<code>']; → next validate locks. revoked_at = null restores."
      v1_caveat: "client lease still lives in IndexedDB, so a wipe BETWEEN downloads can reset locally — but the server row now re-locks it on the next validate (trial-used). Full client-trust removal would need a server-trusted clock on every play, out of scope."

    progress:
      state: "offlineDlState: idle | preparing | downloading | complete | partial | error | locked  (partial = READY, straggler tail retrying in background; locked = lease paused, reconnect to renew)"
      counts: "offlineDlDone / offlineDlTotal / offlineDlFailed (only genuine cache writes tick done; pct uses Math.floor so 9732/9742 reads 99%, never a false 100%)"
      readiness_threshold: >
        resolveOfflineDlOutcome(done,total,failed,auxIncomplete): readiness is a
        THRESHOLD (OFFLINE_READY_MIN_FRACTION = 0.98), never complete==total.
        failed=0 → complete; coverage ≥ threshold → partial (green "Ready
        offline (N clips retrying)", full green ring); below → error — whose
        copy reports true counts and "retrying in background", never blames
        signal. Both partial and error schedule a background straggler retry in
        LearningPlayer (30s/2m/5m, fresh bulkDownloadAudio over the failedIds;
        success promotes to complete). Offline stays ON and playable in every
        outcome — the founder invariant (2026-07-31): always play what you
        have, never an offline dead-end. Probe: e2e/offline-straggler-probe.mjs.
      liveness: >
        "Silently stuck forever" is a forbidden UI state: if no progress event
        (state change or counter tick) lands for OFFLINE_DL_STALL_MS (20s)
        while downloading, offlineDownloadStalled flips and the label/headline
        change to "Stalled at N% (done/total) — retrying…" with real counts.
        A 5s interval (running only while downloading) drives the stall clock;
        the per-fetch timeouts guarantee the machinery itself unsticks within
        ~30s, so the stalled copy is a bridge, never a resting state.
      shared_state: >
        useOfflineDownloadStatus.ts — module-level refs (offlineDlState/Done/Total/
        Failed) + computeds (offlineDownloadVisible/Active/Pct/Label), written by
        LearningPlayer.downloadForOffline, read by ModeTray. Same shared-singleton
        pattern as usePwaUpdate (no prop-drilling to the mode button). LearningPlayer
        resetOfflineDownloadStatus() onMounted + offlineActive=false onUnmounted so a
        course-change remount can't leave a stale ring or an orphaned write loop.
      indicator: >
        A progress RING around the mode-tray trigger button (where offline is
        switched on), NOT a floating banner. Shown when offlineDownloadVisible
        (state≠idle): determinate arc = offlineDownloadPct while downloading, green
        full ring on complete (~4s then idle), red on error, indeterminate spin while
        preparing. pointer-events:none so it never blocks the button. The granular
        "Downloading… N% (x/y)" detail shows on the tray's Offline row (open the tray
        for it) — green while active, red on error.

    # premium_gate + expiry_30_day: BUILT (see premium_gate + offline_lease sections above).

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## GRACEFUL DEGRADATION (INFINITE PLAY)
  ## ==========================================================================

  graceful_degradation:
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useOfflinePlay.ts"
    purpose: "Never-fail playback - always keep playing"

    degradation_hierarchy:
      level_1_normal:
        condition: "Scheduled cycle is cached or online"
        action: "Play scheduled cycle"

      level_2_belt_only:
        condition: "Scheduled unavailable, other cycles cached"
        action: "Play random cached cycle (avoiding recent)"
        message: "Playing from your offline library"

      level_3_use_phrases:
        condition: "Limited cache, only mastered content"
        action: "Play mastered USE phrases"
        message: "Reviewing mastered content while offline"

      level_4_repeat:
        condition: "Minimal cache"
        action: "Repeat last successfully played cycle"
        message: "Repeating last lesson - go online to continue"

    guarantee: "User NEVER sees connection error - audio keeps playing"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## DATA FLOW
  ## ==========================================================================

  data_flow:
    playback:
      description: "How audio gets to the user (online == offline, cache-first)"
      flow: |
        Cycle.audioUrl (/api/audio/<id>)
          → resolveAudioUrl / createAudioCacheSource (shouldServeBlobs = offline || cachePlayOnline)
          → audioCache.getWavBlobUrl(id)  # decode cached mp3 → WAV blob: URL, decoded once
          → HIT:  play the WAV blob from cache (no network, lock-safe)
          → MISS: fall through to /api/audio/<id> (origin proxy, 206 ranges) and stream
                  that one clip while the rolling filler warms the cache behind it

    fill:
      description: "How the cache is kept ahead (the network's only job)"
      flow: |
        Round advance / stop / first-rounds-load
          → fillBuffer(span) via fillRollingBuffer (20min, gentle) or warmBurst (10min, fast)
          → expandScript / ensureLiveSpanLoaded grows the loaded script DEEP
          → ordered missing-list [cycles…, pods…, L1…], dedupe, drain front-to-back
          → audioCache.persistent.ensure(id)  # fetch /api/audio/<id>, store mp3 blob
          → (SimplePlayer.prefetchNextCycle warms the very next cycle's clips)

    offline_play:
      description: "How playback continues offline (graceful degradation)"
      flow: |
        Request next cycle
          → Check if scheduled cycle playable (all 3 ids cached)
          → If yes: play normally (WAV blob from cache)
          → If no: degrade to next level (useOfflinePlay)
          → Get cycle from cached pool
          → Play (user unaware of degradation)

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## FILES SUMMARY
  ## ==========================================================================

  files:
    live:
      - path: "api/audio/[audioId].ts"
        purpose: "Vercel serverless proxy (origin, correct 206 ranges)"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/AudioCache.ts (+ AudioCache.types.ts)"
        purpose: "IndexedDB ssi-audio-cache-v2 — persistent (warm) + ephemeral (vestigial) namespaces"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/createAudioCacheSource.ts"
        purpose: "AudioSource adapter over AudioCache (cache-first read path)"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/resolvePlaybackUrl.ts"
        purpose: "resolveCachedPlaybackUrl — shared id → lock-safe playable (WAV) URL"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/wav.ts"
        purpose: "bytesToWavBlob — decode cached mp3 bytes → WAV blob for WebKit <audio>"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue"
        purpose: "Rolling filler (fillBuffer/expandScript), cachePlayOnline gate, RealAudioController, offline depth picker"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/SimplePlayer.ts"
        purpose: "Spotify-style player — single <audio>, prefetchNextCycle"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useOfflinePlay.ts"
        purpose: "Graceful degradation hierarchy (never-fail)"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useOfflineDownloadStatus.ts"
        purpose: "Module-level shared offline-download progress state (mode-button ring)"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/config/audioConfig.ts"
        purpose: "Audio URL builder and config"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/vite.config.js"
        purpose: "VitePWA/Workbox SW — app shell + fonts only; NO audio"

    deleted_2026_06_08_and_earlier:
      - "packages/core/src/cache/OfflineCache.ts (→ AudioCache)"
      - "packages/core/src/cache/AudioSource.ts (→ createAudioCacheSource)"
      - "packages/core/src/cache/DownloadManager.ts (resumable downloads — gone; depth picker downloadForOffline replaces it)"
      - "packages/core/src/cache/types.ts"
      - "packages/player-vue/src/cache/AudioPrefetcher.ts (no-op since 2026-05-23)"
      - "packages/player-vue/src/cache/BundleDownloader.ts (always-on full-course download — never fired)"
      - "packages/player-vue/src/composables/usePrefetchManager.ts (30-min buffer mgr → rolling filler)"
      - "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useOfflineCache.ts"
      - "supabase/migrations/...audio_plays.sql (table dropped 2026-05-19 — proxy is not a play log)"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## QUALITY METRICS
  ## ==========================================================================

  quality_targets:
    never_fail: "Audio must ALWAYS play, regardless of network"
    atomic_binding: "Text and audio ALWAYS match (Cycle ensures this)"
    cache_first: "The player only ever reads from the cache; the network only fills it ahead"
    buffer_target: "~20 min of cycles (+pods+L1) warmed ahead of the playhead (ROLLING_SPAN_MS)"
    lock_safe: "Main cycle plays cached WAV blobs (not streamed ranges) so it survives iOS lock/background"
    offline_capability: "Deliberate depth picker downloads N% of remaining course; INF PLAY recycles forever"
    analytics_coverage: "Plays tracked client-side via player_events.audio_play (NOT the proxy)"
    eviction: "persistent LRU size-cap (persistentEvictToTarget) + quota self-trim before the browser errors"
